AB  - Complex multi-step tasks such as scientific research are increasingly being performed using LLM-based agents. Existing approaches use fixed agent architectures requiring manual adaptation, or generate individual functions without coordination logic. We present a framework that generates complete multi-agent systems as executable multi-agent system code from natural language descriptions. Our approach employs a seven-stage pipeline with two feedback loops to catch errors at different cost points. On the GAIA benchmark, the framework achieves 49% accuracy on Level 1, 24.4% on Level 2, and 15.4% on Level 3, outperforming the MAS-GPT baseline across all levels.
