AB  - Large language models (LLMs) perform well on general code generation but often struggle with domain-specific software tasks due to limited specialized knowledge in their training data. We propose DomAgent, an autonomous coding agent that enables domain-adapted code generation through structured reasoning and targeted retrieval. Its core module, DomRetriever, combines knowledge-graph reasoning with case-based reasoning to iteratively retrieve and synthesize relevant domain knowledge and examples. Experiments on the DS-1000 benchmark and real-world Volvo truck software development tasks show that DomAgent significantly improves domain-specific code generation, allowing small open-source models to approach the performance of large proprietary LLMs.
